{
  "dom_id": "step-q128053",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is the value of $(-7)÷(-\\frac{14}{3})?$",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a negative number by a negative number gives a positive number. Hence, the result will be positive.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n7÷\\frac{14}{3}=\\frac{7\\times 3}{14}=\\frac{21}{14}=\\frac{3}{2},\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n(-7)÷(-\\frac{14}{3})=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$",
